# clang-tidy check set, run by `make tidy` (the commit gate) - see AGENTS.md.
# Findings are triaged one by one: fix the code, or a // NOLINT(check) at the
# site. No check-wide disables here without an attached reason.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,
  cert-*,
  misc-*,
  readability-function-size,
  readability-inconsistent-declaration-parameter-name,
  readability-suspicious-call-argument
# bugprone-signed-bitwise is off: the codebase composes demod-flag enums
# (demod.h), shifts the bit-clock transition history, bit-reverses FFT
# indices, and byte-swaps/packs raw samples in mw_bench — all on `int`,
# because C integer promotion makes `uint8_t << 4` signed regardless of the
# operand types. The check targets C++ signed shift/mask overflow; in C these
# operations are well-defined at the magnitudes used, and qualifying every
# site unsigned would be churn without safety. If a bitwise bug is ever
# suspected, re-enable the check and triage afresh.
CheckOptions:
  # glibc's errno.h and time.h are thin wrappers over asm-generic/errno* and
  # bits/time internals (EPIPE, EAGAIN, EINTR, ESTRPIPE, CLOCK_BOOTTIME come
  # from there), but include-cleaner can't walk up to the public header and
  # demands the non-self-contained kernel/bits files. Never suggest those;
  # <errno.h> / <time.h> are the correct providers as included.
  - key: misc-include-cleaner.IgnoreHeaders
    value: 'asm-generic/.*|bits/.*'
